{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e","id":896616,"title":"Besides a Solar, what can you currently play in 3E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-23T00:48:07-07:00","id":896616,"title":"Besides a Solar, what can you currently play in 3E?","content":"So, I have a slight boggle. I have a full Circle of Solars. I'd like to add another player, but I really dislike redundancy.<br /> <br /> Is there currently anything I can give him to play wherein he can hang with a Solar Circle and have enough stuff to buy and do to not be bored? I'll accept homebrews, whatever. Has anyone experimented with playable Gods?<br /> <br /> If there aren't, I'll ask my players if anyone of them is willing to share their Caste, but I'd like to avoid that if I can.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> And I don't mean any flavor of mortal. Has to be someone who can survive and excel in shit like fights with Deathlords and First Age Lunars. Even God-Blooded feel a bit weak for what I'm doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11816,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","user":"Foxcalibur","date":".  No mortals need apply. Irish are fine. If they're Exalted. 05-23-2016, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:05:00-07:00","id":896621,"title":"","content":"Heroic Mortals using the rules given in the character creation chapter. God-Blooded, if you throw on some supernatural merits. Mortal Sorcerer, if you follow the rules in the Sorcery section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:12:21-07:00","id":896624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896621#post896621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroic Mortals using the rules given in the character creation chapter. God-Blooded, if you throw on some supernatural merits. Mortal Sorcerer, if you follow the rules in the Sorcery section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally a valid suggestion, but definitely too weak for the sort of content they'll be facing. I appreciate the suggestion, though. Clarified my original post to avoid further upmixes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:29:08-07:00","id":896631,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew\"><b>Sidereal Update Homebrew</b> (<b>Grifftofer)</b></a><br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/posts/4128715/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sidereal Hombrew (Irked)</b></a><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\">Lunar Charms for 3e (Irked)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/736291-alchemical-3e-conversion\">Alchemical 3e conversion</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/736291-alchemical-3e-conversion\"> (Sandact6)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/815113-ex3-raziere-s-infernal-homebrew\">Infernal Homebrew (Raziere)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\">Dragon Kings homebrew (Lanaya)</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:57:22-07:00","id":896643,"title":"","content":"It's just Solars and heroic mortals and whatever you want to homebrew right now. That said, a sixth Solar is not necessarily redundant given the number of Charms available now and how Supernal works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T02:00:36-07:00","id":896645,"title":"","content":"(Alternately you could use wasteven's <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?780702-Exalted-3-Tinkering-with-a-fan-supplements-Sidereals-Where-Fate-Has-Led\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereals: Where Fate Has Lead homebrew</a>.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T02:00:47-07:00","id":896646,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's got to be <i>something</i> none of your current players are focused on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T02:03:51-07:00","id":896648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896646#post896646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's got to be <i>something</i> none of your current players are focused on.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agreed. Solars have the most variety, freedom, and power of any splat, there must be a hundred different things your current circle aren't doing, and a thousand ways to do them that this guy could help out with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T02:07:14-07:00","id":896650,"title":"","content":"In my game, there are 2 Eclipses, a Dawn, a Zenith and a Twilight (and a Casteless Lunar and a Full Moon). We would have had 3 Eclipses, had not one retired (he's just started playing the Dawn).<br /> The two Eclipses do not feel similar at all.<br /> One is a princess who rides a dragon, has an army of gryffon riders, wields a huge golden sword, shoots fire, summons demons and elementals, and rules a mountain kingdom led by scaly people bound to her by blood magic.<br /> The other is a wandering anarcho-feminist revolutionary.<br /> <br /> So, Stephenis is right, I wouldn't worry about redundancy too much, it's pretty easy to have very different kinds of characters (especially Eclipses and Twilights; the Twilight in my game is a doctor/crafter, so if someone else played a sorcerer I doubt they'd feel similar).<br /> <br /> Though of course, if you'd like, there are a number of homebrews for other kinds of Exalts.<br /> How much XP do your players have? I think playing a homebrew character is easier for low-xp games than high-xp games (although my PCs are Essence 5 and include 2 Lunars).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T02:41:02-07:00","id":896657,"title":"","content":"To put it another way: Having two Dawns is not like having two Fighters in 3e or 5e D&amp;D. It's like having two people with the Martial power origin in 4e. The most important points of redundancy to be concerned with are overall concept [there's roughly 10 listed per caste], Supernal ability [MA is basically the only exception in that two people could go for totally different sets of styles], and choices of favored/caste abilities.<br /> <br /> With Solars' ability to choose five of eight caste, you can have two Dawns with basically nothing in common except that they both consider, say, Dodge, Awareness, and War to be Caste and both share the same Anima effect. One's a man-at-arms with Melee and Resistance, a heavily armored mercenary who's just been thrust into the role of commanding his warband after he took the fallen pennant and led them to victory; another's a street tough with Brawl and Thrown who finds herself able to stand up to the oppressive satrap's men rather than skulking in the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T03:14:25-07:00","id":896663,"title":"","content":"You could use my DB stuff, but I only have four and a half Charm sets so far, so selection is limited. I'll be freed up to work on them soon and I aim to be finished by the end of July.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 05-25-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T03:39:02-07:00","id":896670,"title":"","content":"Don't have a game yet (Literally got the Book/PDF on thursday....) But i do have afew dozen different Characters to try/Build.. some might be similar to others.. but That's just my way of building/thinking.<br /> <br /> Dawn's: A Warlord who command's a Group of Mercenaries (Standard Faire). A Scout/Archer who focuses on ranged combat while capable of melee (Abit of a Narcissist, Doesn't want to get his/her clothes Ruined). A Dawn Caste Sorcerer who uses his/her spells to set-up the battlefield for his/her group to have the homefield advantage (Uses Brawl as a back-up to the spells so to as not be &quot;Helpless&quot;).<br /> Night's: A Showboating rabblerouser who sometimes sneaks about and arranges for places to be open when they shouldn't be, avoids conflict asmuch as possible but will still fight if cornered (Uses alot of Improvised weapons rather then carrying armed). A Pious Immaculate Monk who has warped the teachings into something new, as such to place the Solars as the ultimate expression of the Immaculate Faith (Uses charms to confuse and twist other peoples faith in ways similar to their own). A Former Thug who mugs people in broad daylight and disappears without leaving clues behind (Only Mugs from the Guild or Dynasts has made themselves into a Combat BEAST with afew charms to get away/hide in ambush).<br /> <br /> Eclipse's are the Most broad possible for concepts and Zenith i find least inspiring (Personal preference) Twilight's can also be interesting to make into things they usually aren't...<br /> <br /> Sorry think i went on a bit of a of topic Rant.... From what i've seen it's Heroic Mortals, Thumatages/Sorcerers and Solars MAYBE a Godblooded or similar if you can Hack them from the Corebook at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:12:44-07:00","id":896698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896670#post896670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zenith i find least inspiring</div> </div> </div> </div>That is almost unspeakably ironic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:31:58-07:00","id":896707,"title":"","content":"And yet, judging from how often I see Zeniths played compared to other castes, it's clearly a common opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:32:50-07:00","id":896708,"title":"","content":"Edit: Double Post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:01:37-07:00","id":896726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896698#post896698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is almost unspeakably ironic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically... I Didn't see the Irony until you pointed it out. I Can think of Concepts for them but... I Have to force them, or try harder then normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:24:26-07:00","id":896736,"title":"","content":"They're the only caste that can get survival or performance as supernal. So that opens up two archetypes right there: the old Beastmaster archetype as well as a bunch of entertainer types.<br /> <br /> They're the only ones who can take the &quot;seduce everyone in the room through exotic dance&quot; charm at character generation, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:29:08-07:00","id":896742,"title":"","content":"The thing is, they're presented as Old Testament Prophets, for whom seducing everyone in the room through exotic dance, or being a beastmaster tbh, isn't really something that jumps out. Whereas Twilights are presented as the really clever guys, which is a much wider conceptual space.<br /> <br /> I find the best Zenith character concepts I can come up with generally come when I abandon the idea of &quot;priest of the Unconquered Sun.&quot; And, for that matter, so have the most interesting Zenith concepts I've seen played by others. I mean, one of my players is right now, playing a fairly straight-up priest of the Unconquered Sun, and in doing so I think fills a certain role in the party in an interesting way. But it's more the way the others react to him that's interesting, than he himself, who I would say is less interesting than that player's previous tyrant-lizard-riding Djala alchemist, or another players' Zenith priest of a minor forest god.<br /> <br /> I do find, overall, that Zeniths are the hardest caste for me to think of interesting concepts for. That has little to do with their caste abilities though, and much more to do with their narrative role and anima powers (as their anima powers reinforce a specific narrative role more than other castes' do).<br /> I'm not saying I dislike them, just that I find it difficult to think of ways to do Zeniths in an original and interesting way, compared to other castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-23-2016, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:40:46-07:00","id":896751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e#post896616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a slight boggle. I have a full Circle of Solars. I'd like to add another player, but I really dislike redundancy.<br /> <br /> Is there currently anything I can give him to play wherein he can hang with a Solar Circle and have enough stuff to buy and do to not be bored? I'll accept homebrews, whatever. Has anyone experimented with playable Gods?<br /> <br /> If there aren't, I'll ask my players if anyone of them is willing to share their Caste, but I'd like to avoid that if I can.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> And I don't mean any flavor of mortal. Has to be someone who can survive and excel in shit like fights with Deathlords and First Age Lunars. Even God-Blooded feel a bit weak for what I'm doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think everyone has already offered the most complete fan projects. I have a few other suggestions.<br /> <br /> My experience with Ex3 so far is that while Castes are more sharply demarcated, role and concept are fuzzier. Let me unpack that a bit.<br /> <br /> For Solars, Supernal is limited to Caste, and Supernal is intended to &quot;define the legend of that Exalt.&quot; So, characters defined as &quot;Crafter&quot; or &quot;Doctor,&quot; are going to be Twilight, for example.<br /> However, what I have found is that many of the Abilities just don't lend themselves to being Supernal. War is a good example of this. It has few charms overall, and no charms at E4 or 5.<br /> <br /> The net result for Solars is some characters are defined by Supernal, but most are some degree of generalist or hybrid specialist. A Dawn Caste who builds around Melee, Thrown, and War is going to feel very, very different from one who builds around Brawl/MA Supernal. So different, in fact, that I doubt they would conceptually step on each other much (other than they both fight things, and don't most Exalts fight to one extent or another?).<br /> <br /> This brings me to another point. Some &quot;concepts&quot; are just really big. Martial Arts and Sorcery are conceptually and mechanically broad enough that they can sustain a character concept all on their own. MA has enough neat tricks and combinations that a character who invests heavily will always have something to bring to the party. Sorcery, assuming you are willing to update spells to 3rd Edition, is also pretty broad, because a Sorcerer can do Workings to enhance the party, make minions, alter terrain, etc.<br /> <br /> So, the new Caste Ability spreads for 3rd didn't just give a little wiggle room to the Castes themselves. They unlocked completely different ways of approaching the Caste in question.<br /> <br /> Example Twilight concepts (for funsies):<ul><li>Pokemaster (Twilight Anima power+Survival charms and Sorcery for Summoning/Workings)</li> <li>Crafter (you can spend every point of applicable XP from E1 to E5 and STILL have charms to buy)</li> <li>Lore Master (or as a friend put it, a Burning Crusade-era Shadow Priest. Lore also has a crap-ton of charms.)</li> <li>Martial Sorcerer (MA+Sorcery for ISoB and WDC)</li> <li>Cat Burglar Twilight (Stealth, Larceny, and the Twilight anima to pop out after infiltrating and acquiring loot)</li> <li>THE Sorcerer (Summon Demons, pour XP into Workings to augment the party and self, and wreck BGs with DoOB)</li> <li>Sherlock Motherfuckin' Holmes (Investigation+Bureaucracy+Presence+Socialize)</li> </ul>All of those characters can/ought to be Twilight, but they are different enough that I don't think they will step on each other at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:41:09-07:00","id":896752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896742#post896742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, they're presented as Old Testament Prophets, for whom seducing everyone in the room through exotic dance, or being a beastmaster tbh, isn't really something that jumps out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know... it can make me think a bit of the Song of Solomon and John the Baptist.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think with Zeniths, it's generally a case of... magnetic personality isn't the centre of it, it's an aspect in service to the narrative of the hero as righteous exemplar and inspirational leader, but the magnetic personality stuff can be focused on to a degree that doesn't need to constantly reference the righteousness and inspiration.<br /> <br /> Although I do think it's a pity that people tend to be down on the idea of Zeniths as actual spiritual leaders and founders of religions; even from a secular perspective, I think they often make for fascinating historical figures.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:44:13-07:00","id":896754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896742#post896742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, they're presented as Old Testament Prophets\u2026 being a beastmaster tbh, isn't really something that jumps out.</div> </div> </div> </div>II Kings 2:23-24: &quot;Some kids called me bald? <i>Summon the bears!!</i>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-23-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:49:13-07:00","id":896760,"title":"","content":"@ Wizard, i would argue that they would work just as well as the Judges from the Old Testament, i could for example see Sampson as a Zenth, Gideon and Deborah too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2080-protector152","name":"Protector152","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:08:51-07:00","id":896772,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough, of the 8 games I've ever played/GMed, we have only once ever NOT had a Zenith (and that was a 2 person game with an Eclipse and a Full-Moon). So mileage may vary. <br /> <br /> I agree with previous statements about having 2 of the same caste not being that redundant. My current group is a Dawn Martial Artist/Investigator, a Zenith Performer/Scam Artist (sorry, &quot;Business woman&quot;), and 2 Nights, a Daredevil-styled head of a local gang, and a streetwise drifter master-thief who does it for the pleasure. Other then both being related to the criminal element, the two Nights are very different people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:23:39-07:00","id":896788,"title":"","content":"For an upcoming game of mine, two players are making Twilights - one is a Loremaster who used his knowledge of history and geography to puzzle out the location of a Singing Staff, which he uses for architecture; the other is an escaped slave who was taught sorcery by an elemental who shared the same master as her. <br /> <br /> They're very drastically different despite both having Lore, Craft, Occult, and Performance as some of their most key Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:36:53-07:00","id":896801,"title":"","content":"So far as I know, the only options available, as of the core release, is only Solar, or mortal. That said, there's a number of good homebrew projects in the works. I'm a bit hesitant to just pick up 'charm selections' as a homebrew, but that said, Wastevens has one of the most complete conversions I've seen so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:56:01-07:00","id":896814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Protector152</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896760#post896760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Wizard, i would argue that they would work just as well as the Judges from the Old Testament, i could for example see Sampson as a Zenth, Gideon and Deborah too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, they're perfect as Old Testament prophets: Integrity even has a charm just for Samson. What I find more difficult is to play them as <i>not</i> Old Testament prophets.<br /> <br /> This possibly is connected to the fact that I don't like playing stereotypical castes. I'd rather play a fat but brilliant general Dawn than a swordsman; an actor or a Conan-esque barbarian than an assassin Night; uneducated shaman or a big burly blacksmith than a scholar/sorcerer Twilight. So I'd rather play an ancestor cultist, ex-monk struggling to reconcile his Immaculate faith with being a demon, or a dissolute wastrel soldier who exalts as a Zenith because he drunkely fought demons, than an Old Testament Prophet. But somehow, I find it harder to play something that's off the core concept of Zeniths than with other castes. Maybe it's the way that they are all, metaphysically, priests of the Unconquered Sun, in a way that not all Dawns are soldiers and not all Nights are thieves? I'm not sure. TBH, I'd much rather play a priest or monk of basically any other religion than the UCS.<br /> Also, those who are not priests (like Karal Fire Orchid or Ocean Pearl) are leaders, and I don't like playing leaders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">II Kings 2:23-24: &quot;Some kids called me bald? <i>Summon the bears!!</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor Elisha. He does it one time and no-one lets him forget.<br /> (Anyway... he's not bonded with animals. He just curses them with the judgement of Heaven. Which is bears.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know... it can make me think a bit of the Song of Solomon and John the Baptist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely John the Baptist is a lesson in the dangers of seductive dancing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think with Zeniths, it's generally a case of... magnetic personality isn't the centre of it, it's an aspect in service to the narrative of the hero as righteous exemplar and inspirational leader, but the magnetic personality stuff can be focused on to a degree that doesn't need to constantly reference the righteousness and inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm... I think there's something good here, but I'm not sure where to go with it.<br /> <br /> Maybe... you can play a Zenith who is an inspiring political orator, not righteous.* (Though this doesn't quite fit the priest/prophet angle).<br /> <br /> And maybe you can play a Zenith who is a straight-up righteous hero*, but who lacks preaching skills. Moses-esque**. Or Captain America. =3rd ed definitely makes it easier, since you can not take Performance/Personality.<br /> <br /> * I very much dislike the idea of a &quot;righteous&quot; caste. People playing &quot;good&quot; characters goes very badly 90% of the time in my experience. This is one part I find difficult about Zeniths. If you look in the Aspect Book Zenith, they're basically all good people. There's not even any fanatics. That's pretty difficult to live up to.<br /> <br /> I should say... this is not me saying I hate Zeniths. It's more me asking for help, because I find them difficult to make in an interesting way, and I need to make a new character as I've just retired my Lunar (and Zenith is the caste we're missing).<br /> <br /> I did actually play a Zenith recently: a young mutant barbarian ex-slave whose goal (on a pirate ship) was to free all slaves. I felt the worthy goal meant I could fit the &quot;righteous&quot; perspective without her necessarily having to be a righteous person generally. Not sure what similar goal I could put into the game I'm playing now. If we had an occupying enemy army, I could oppose them, but we don't.<br /> Unfortunately, the game died out quickly.<br /> <br /> **Hmmm... this actually makes me think of the unwilling hero. Odyssues, Moses, Jonah (my favourite Prophet).<br /> Much as I dislike electionism... it could work. A random guy, gets picked by the UCS, but that doesn't mean he wants to preach about the UCS, but, as happens with PCs, he just keeps running into things that force him back onto the hero's path. People in trouble. Random demons. Hmmm... not sure about this, but it's something to consider. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I do think it's a pity that people tend to be down on the idea of Zeniths as actual spiritual leaders and founders of religions; even from a secular perspective, I think they often make for fascinating historical figures.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do... but I find that Zeniths never do found their own religions, nor are they ever presented as doing so. It's always a matter of restoring the UCS's worship, not making something new (they seem more like OT Prophets than they are Jesus, Muhammed, Buddha, etc).<br /> (One might argue out that Jesus wasn't trying to make something new necessarily, but in practice he did, because his interpretation of the true worship of Jehovah was radically different from the two mainstream Jewish sects. I never see Zeniths doing anything like that. I mean, how many deep discussions of theology do Zeniths seem to do in the fluff? It seems very much like that's a thing that Immaculate Monks do, but not a thing Zeniths do.)<br /> I'd love to see some Zeniths making their own religions. That would certainly inspire me to play one more.<br /> Currently, I find Immaculates far more fascinating than Zeniths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-23-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:13:17-07:00","id":896825,"title":"","content":"If a Zenith doesn't do something in the fluff, and you feel like they should, then maybe make that character and do that thing.<br /> <br /> I thought the Nameless Solar, the Righteous Devil was a Zenith, but apparently I thought wrong. Anyway, a gunslinger/hellfire preacher may also be a good Zenith, especially one not interested at all in leading or even worship, but in sin, and the burning thereof. Which is not that much different from a traditional DnD Paladin, come to think of it; Zenith have what is basically Smite Evil as an anima power.<br /> <br /> I wanted to recreate Virgo Shaka of Saint Seiya fame as a Zenith, but the lack of charms that send people to illusionary Samsaras and blasting them with sunlit telekinetic energy and floating in mid-air with one's eyes closed was disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:13:49-07:00","id":896826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896742#post896742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, they're presented as Old Testament Prophets, for whom seducing everyone in the room through exotic dance, or being a beastmaster tbh, isn't really something that jumps out. Whereas Twilights are presented as the really clever guys, which is a much wider conceptual space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Zenith concepts that I have in mind is some kind of performers since most of the Christian stuffs kinda fly over my head :'P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:15:12-07:00","id":896829,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a><br /> <br /> Righteousness doesn't really mean good. It just means the Zenith believes what they are doing is right, and right is often subjective.<br /> <br /> So, a Zenith can righteously invade some nice land, slaughter its inhabitants, and settle his people on it. His people benefit, so he's remembered as a great hero.<br /> <br /> And priest can mean many things, and doesn't have to include the baggage of Abrahamic Monotheist-type holy people. Maybe the Zenith's faith is intensely personal, and he wants to work his will on the world, and make it work in accordance with his perception of UCS's desires, rather than just convert people. He doesn't preach about Sol; he speechifies about freedom.<br /> <br /> The nice thing about 3rd Edition and the gods is the character can say just about anything is &quot;what Sol wants,&quot; and have it be true, at least true enough.<br /> <br /> In making a Zenith, I wouldn't say &quot;how do I make a priest?&quot; I would say &quot;what do I want this character to do?&quot; and then I would take the &quot;righteousness&quot; and layer that on top","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  typo 05-23-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:16:18-07:00","id":896830,"title":"","content":"While most Zeniths are priests, it's easier to think of them as the hero in the hero journey. It isn't bad in itself but Zenith essentially are all your inspirational leader heroes archetypes (A very common trope in cartoons, movies and the shonen genre of anime, the hero type mostly), some have crisis of faith depending on which god they worship, others still follow the gods that they had before they became solar...as you can do whatever you want with exaltation.<br /> <br /> For various concept in creation for Zeniths:<br /> Priest of the Old Temples, City Elder, Servant of the Syndics, Immaculate Missionary, Northern Scout, Dream Interpreter, Speaker with the Dead, Priests of the Deathlords, Shamans, Mystics, Reformed Tomb Robber, Animal Trainer, Nobles, hell even a lintha family leader etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:17:42-07:00","id":896831,"title":"","content":"I made a Zenith who is a holy Honey Hunter for a coastal empire in the south desperatly trying to curb the decadance of his homeland. I really hope to actually play him someday","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:21:23-07:00","id":896833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The net result for Solars is some characters are defined by Supernal, but most are some degree of generalist or hybrid specialist. A Dawn Caste who builds around Melee, Thrown, and War is going to feel very, very different from one who builds around Brawl/MA Supernal. So different, in fact, that I doubt they would conceptually step on each other much (other than they both fight things, and don't most Exalts fight to one extent or another?).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I find very important when players start fretting about characters having similar abilities.<br /> Some things can feel niche-stealy when two PCs have it. For example, you flee to the river and need to escape quickly on a boat. The Night-caste Pirate steps forward and says &quot;time to break out my Sail charms! Awesome!&quot; And then the Eclipse does the same too. Redundant.<br /> On the other hand, combat abilities are virtually never redundant, because fights generally involve all the PCs anyway. Occult is largely similar: after all, in a fight against spirits, everyone's going to be fighting the spirits if they can (not all Occult charms are about fighting spirits of course... but the majority are). And it's useful for multiple people to have some social skills, because sometimes other people want to speak besides the Face. Last session several of my players decided they needed to buy Performance, because you can't rely on the Zenith to do all your talking for you, when other PCs have different opinions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This brings me to another point. Some &quot;concepts&quot; are just really big. Martial Arts and Sorcery are conceptually and mechanically broad enough that they can sustain a character concept all on their own. MA has enough neat tricks and combinations that a character who invests heavily will always have something to bring to the party. Sorcery, assuming you are willing to update spells to 3rd Edition, is also pretty broad, because a Sorcerer can do Workings to enhance the party, make minions, alter terrain, etc. </div> </div> </div>My game includes a Celestial sorcerer and Solar sorcerer, and they both are useful to the party. They know different spells for the most part, but also workings take a long time, so two of them means they can do two workings at once.<br /> And MA, of course, is really a whole bunch of different charm sets.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:30:49-07:00","id":896841,"title":"","content":"Other Zenith concepts I would list would be Sadhu (wandering ascetics and holy men), Shaolin-type monks, Mohist philosophers, Bene Gesserit, mendicant knights, Ji Gong the Mad Monk, aaaaaaaand...Steven Universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:40:06-07:00","id":896847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896826#post896826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Zenith concepts that I have in mind is some kind of performers since most of the Christian stuffs kinda fly over my head :'P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if you're happy with that, good for you. It's the Judeo-Christian influences that I find difficult to reconcile with other parts of the Zenith concept.<br /> I actually do have some concepts for performers, but they're always much more Nights or Eclipses than they are Zeniths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Righteousness doesn't really mean good. It just means the Zenith believes what they are doing is right, and right is often subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so. It's something I'd like to see more of in the fluff. As I mentioned, of the Caste books, the Zeniths come off as by far the most objectively good, not the ones with the strongest beliefs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And priest can mean many things, and doesn't have to include the baggage of Abrahamic Monotheist-type holy people. Maybe the Zenith's faith is intensely personal, and he wants to work his will on the world, and make it work in accordance with his perception of UCS's desires, rather than just convert people. He doesn't preach about Sol; he speechifies about freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not precisely the issue for me... I mean, lots of Abrahamic Monotheist-type holy people's faith was intensely personal. And I do find many of them interesting historical/mythical people, but not because of their preaching. What I mean is, I find St Paul interesting as a theologian and reformed anti-Christian fanatic thug/murderer, not as a Zenith-esque preaching figure. And I find monks very interesting, I like Immaculate Monks (who are more based on Buddhist monks, but still). I did think about playing a Zenith as a scholarly monk (which wasn't really a thing that would fit very well in 2nd ed, but now they have Lore it might work better).<br /> I guess the issue is that Zeniths are based more on the biblical figures I find less interesting than the ones I find more interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> others still follow the gods that they had before they became solar</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely something I'd like to see more of. The most entertaining Zenith I've seen played was a Zenith who thought the UCS was a loser compared to his awesome minor forest god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:40:59-07:00","id":896848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896831#post896831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a Zenith who is a holy Honey Hunter for a coastal empire in the south desperatly trying to curb the decadance of his homeland. I really hope to actually play him someday</div> </div> </div> </div>So... he hunts honey? For the god of bees? I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:44:02-07:00","id":896849,"title":"","content":"&quot;Bees? My god!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, <i>my </i>god.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T09:55:16-07:00","id":896888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896825#post896825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Zenith doesn't do something in the fluff, and you feel like they should, then maybe make that character and do that thing.<br /> <br /> I thought the Nameless Solar, the Righteous Devil was a Zenith, but apparently I thought wrong. Anyway, a gunslinger/hellfire preacher may also be a good Zenith, especially one not interested at all in leading or even worship, but in sin, and the burning thereof. Which is not that much different from a traditional DnD Paladin, come to think of it; Zenith have what is basically Smite Evil as an anima power.<br /> <br /> I wanted to recreate Virgo Shaka of Saint Seiya fame as a Zenith, but the lack of charms that send people to illusionary Samsaras and blasting them with sunlit telekinetic energy and floating in mid-air with one's eyes closed was disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will Shattering Illusion for mind trap and Ascendant Battle Visage (with extras) for sunlit telekinetic blasts. The blasts could be many things actually.<br /> <br /> But the mind trap is pretty clear. The meditation in this case 8s just description cause the meditation charms are non agressive.<br /> <br /> Rest is stunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:02:03-07:00","id":896892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896847#post896847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not precisely the issue for me... I mean, lots of Abrahamic Monotheist-type holy people's faith was intensely personal. And I do find many of them interesting historical/mythical people, but not because of their preaching. What I mean is, I find St Paul interesting as a theologian and reformed anti-Christian fanatic thug/murderer, not as a Zenith-esque preaching figure. And I find monks very interesting, I like Immaculate Monks (who are more based on Buddhist monks, but still). I did think about playing a Zenith as a scholarly monk (which wasn't really a thing that would fit very well in 2nd ed, but now they have Lore it might work better).<br /> I guess the issue is that Zeniths are based more on the biblical figures I find less interesting than the ones I find more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you speaking in terms of the canon Zeniths on offer, or what you feel is the conceptual space of Zeniths in general? If you're speaking of the former, I tend to agree (right down to Panther being the loud, black preacher who shouts about his sins). If the latter, I think you can do a lot more with them than that.<br /> <br /> Or maybe this is more about the &quot;leader&quot; aspect of Zeniths, and less about the spiritual overtones?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think you can take just about any profession/avocation/political role and make it the core of a Zenith. You just make their defining trait something they believe in, not something they do. A Zenith scholar isn't a scholar because he likes books and knowledge; he <b>knows</b> that knowledge is the key to saving his people, making the world a better place, etc. It's not an intellectual/analytical conclusion, but a matter of faith, the way many people simply know God exists. If you can give the character that gut-level belief in something, they can be Zenith, even if they aren't overtly religious or remotely interesting in traditional leadership.<br /> <br /> Sample of RL Zeniths<br /> Gandhi<br /> Bloody Mary -- faith was the inspiration, or perhaps merely the excuse, for her depredations<br /> Patton -- the man treated warfare as a religion, not simply a calling.<br /> Mao -- uses ideology to win support for himself and fuel his rise to power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:17:11-07:00","id":896904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896631#post896631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew\"><b>Sidereal Update Homebrew</b> (<b>Grifftofer)</b></a><br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/posts/4128715/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sidereal Hombrew (Irked)</b></a><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\">Lunar Charms for 3e (Irked)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/736291-alchemical-3e-conversion\">Alchemical 3e conversion</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/736291-alchemical-3e-conversion\"> (Sandact6)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/815113-ex3-raziere-s-infernal-homebrew\">Infernal Homebrew (Raziere)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\">Dragon Kings homebrew (Lanaya)</a></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also tried doing Infernal homebrew, but due to some IRL issues that has become delayed.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to get back on track and finish it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:42:50-07:00","id":896935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896848#post896848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... he hunts honey? For the god of bees? I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No no its a play on this ancient egyptian thing where these hunters would go out and find honey for their god kings. I made him a supurnal survival it could develop into that but i havent gotten to play him yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:03:16-07:00","id":897096,"title":"","content":"Heck, you can get quite different characters even when focusing on the same Ability. Especially so if your players are fond of making custom Charms, but even using only the published material, some Abilities have various different archetypes on their Charm Trees.<br /> <br /> Example: for a while in my game we had 3 Dawn Castes, all of which were Melee Supernal. Even leaving aside their different personalities (though that plays into their Charm choices), one was a sword and shield dude who protected everyone with Defend Other Charms and smacked would-be attackers with counterattack Charms. Another went for a light weapon and a death-of-a-thousand-cuts speedy style with Multiattack Charms. The third one was a burly dude with a Grand Goremaul and Charms mostly to enhance damage. They all had surprisingly few Charms in common, and their supporting combat Charms from other abilities were also pretty different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:37:23-07:00","id":897120,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> I have a Zenith, Copper Rashi.<br /> <br /> She's Athletics-supernal, a Solar Strongwoman. She's an orator, and a showman, and a very talented 'performer' that can't turn down a pretty face. She has no great cause, and wouldn't want one if it were offered - but she's good at being an ear for people to talk about their problems to, and maybe offering a few words of straightforward advice. She probably couldn't be your therapist, but she'd make a great Central Casting Bartender.<br /> <br /> I think she works as a Zenith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:22:58-07:00","id":897180,"title":"","content":"I think that saying Zeniths are the priests is like saying Dawns are fighters, or that Twilights are sorcerers. Not wrong, but nowhere NEAR the full story.<br /> <br /> To me, the Zeniths <i>inspire</i>. The thing is? This can come in <i>countless</i> ways. A Zenith should, after leaving you life, change you in some way, make you want to be greater. They could speak and convince the commoners to rise up against their oppressors. They could show up and rally the people to rebuild their home in the wake of a disaster.<br /> <br /> The wandering Righteous Devil that came in and cleared out the bandits keeping the town in fear? SHE was a Zenith.<br /> <br /> The nameless man who came through and set all the slaves free, and told them to find their own future? Well that was probably Strength-of-Many. Or it could have been a Zenith.<br /> <br /> The former Dynast who left her old life behind, and now wants to try and make this world better (despite having NO goddamn idea how to start that?) SHE can be a Zenith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:28:42-07:00","id":897188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896904#post896904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I also tried doing Infernal homebrew, but due to some IRL issues that has become delayed.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to get back on track and finish it though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've seen it before, and was wondering/fearing for it's status. It's amazing to hear the project hasn't been abandoned, I have a player at my table reading the google doc we found religiously for use for an infernal in our game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T16:05:55-07:00","id":897292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896829#post896829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a><br /> So, a Zenith can righteously invade some nice land, slaughter its inhabitants, and settle his people on it. His people benefit, so he's remembered as a great hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vlad the Impaler is considered a folk hero in Romania for defending Christendom against the Turks, despite his unusually bloodthirsty efforts at damaging enemy morale and his, shall we say, <i>uniquely ruthless</i> solution to the problems of poverty and hunger in his own country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:15:33-07:00","id":897362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=897188#post897188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've seen it before, and was wondering/fearing for it's status. It's amazing to hear the project hasn't been abandoned, I have a player at my table reading the google doc we found religiously for use for an infernal in our game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I won't lie, it still exists. I originally had it slated for March, but what happened was I learned my father had terminal cancer, which made me feel like shit for nearly all my projects. I'm fine now, but now I want to finish it before my father kicks the bucket and I'll really lose my writing grove for months.<br /> <br /> I tried doing a tiny bit in May, such as simple things like enemy statblocks and a GM guide to get me back into the grove of things... then my town burned down. The massive Canadian Wildfire that was all over the news in the beginning of the month? In Fort McMurray? Yea... At least Edmonton is really nice though.<br /> <br /> It's exactly like all the fallout characters I make with 2-3 Luck. One person I told this to asked me what Sidereal I pissed off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:44:26-07:00","id":897384,"title":"","content":"So, I definitely appreciate everybody's advice to &quot;just have six Solars.&quot; I agree with all statements about the lack of mechanical overlap. Honest and for-truly. My main wish, however, is to avoid thematic overlap and to maintain a trend in my campaign wherein there's only ever one of everything. <br /> <br /> Great advice, really! And I'm open to it if there's no other choice. But it's not ideal for narrative reasons. <br /> <br /> As options go, how well do folks think a Dragon King Ochilike could hold his own with the Solar Exalted at say 150 XP? What if I started him as an Ancient? <br /> <br /> And I really do like the idea of a playable God hanging out with a circle of Solars. Are there any good conversions for Godly charms and an XP table for Gods compatible with 3E that anyone knows of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:57:51-07:00","id":897394,"title":"","content":"Take it from someone who's run many mixed games: Balancing is often going to be a god damn nightmare with many different splat types. Its easier with Celestials, but *do not* use Terrestials mixed with Celestials. This is to only be done by a GM who is well aware of both or a player who REALLY knows the ins and outs of the system. For this example, Dragon Kings are even lower power than Terrestials. I mean they get some nice tricks, but they're a pain in the ass to balance around. 150 XP gives a few more grab bag of tricks and some high abilities/attributes... before you realize that Solars with 50 XP can often blow those out of the water. The only thing that would give them pause is something I toyed around with in something like my Exalted Modern game where Elder DK's turned into literal Western Dragons (Like out of Endless Legend, and even scarier to deal with).<br /> <br /> Gods as characters have never had fully fleshed out sets in exalted, seriously. Even in 2e the advice for making a PC god was basically &quot;Do whatever you think looks cool.&quot; My best advice would be to wait until Exigents for Gods, or just treat Gods as Exigents for simplicity reasons. The only thing a God really swaps around is his anima banner for their spirit nature (Very hard to kill). The God charms in 2e can be ported over, and honestly I'd suggest doing so to save yourself some time in statting things, but for PC's you're making an entire charm set from scratch.<br /> <br /> My honest advice, if you're going to mix things up stick with Exalts. Solars are the only splat that are officially released right now. My Alchemical homebrew I can attest to being relatively balanced (Probably baised, but still). My Infernal homebrew still has a lot of work left, but I heard some crazy people were using that so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:04:35-07:00","id":897443,"title":"","content":"For the OP. One idea would be to pick and exalt type thats not out yet but have them concentrate on Martial Arts and Artifact Evocations until the book comes out. What their exaltation is is irrelevant to their passion for their art and their blade. A combination package would be a worshipper of Mara who know her Sorcerous initiation, has a variant of Wood Dragon's claw called Mara's Claw and know black Claw style. She would have the demonic tattoos and between buying evocations for the claws and tattoos and buying spells and martial arts skills there wouldn't be much left for exalt specific needs. You could even give them abilities from the Infernals book converted into Sorcerous workings inflicted on the character by Mara.<br /> <br /> For the Zenith Discussion: Disney Princesses. They are beautiful, loved by everyone that isn't trying to hate them, the can wander aimlessly through a forbidding wood while still arriving exactly where they need to go, they can command wild life by singing to it, and they can be present in epic battles usually no worse for wear after the hero/prince saves them (who they could very while have inspired (trained with WAR)). I saw it mentioned once but now I just can't unsee it.<br /> <br /> I actually play a Zenith who is basically Link. The Zenith anima effect is how his enemies corpses disappear and leave behind the loot, hurt ghosts, and allow him to call out powerful bosses to battle even when they are really just spirits possessing an object or location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8896-starjaunter","name":"Starjaunter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:18:51-07:00","id":897459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=897292#post897292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vlad the Impaler is considered a folk hero in Romania for defending Christendom against the Turks, despite his unusually bloodthirsty efforts at damaging enemy morale and his, shall we say, <i>uniquely ruthless</i> solution to the problems of poverty and hunger in his own country.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Oftentimes history forgives the ruthless murderous motherfucker who is on the &quot;right&quot; side.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11816_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11816\" data-vbnamecard=\"11816\">Foxcalibur</a> , Are you hoping for near mechanical parity, or just don't want them to be worthless? There is the classic setup of an older Dragon-Blood being the face of a party of Solars, if the player is amenable to loading up on Backgrounds and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:26:19-07:00","id":897465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=897362#post897362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I won't lie, it still exists. I originally had it slated for March, but what happened was I learned my father had terminal cancer, which made me feel like shit for nearly all my projects. I'm fine now, but now I want to finish it before my father kicks the bucket and I'll really lose my writing grove for months.<br /> <br /> I tried doing a tiny bit in May, such as simple things like enemy statblocks and a GM guide to get me back into the grove of things... then my town burned down. The massive Canadian Wildfire that was all over the news in the beginning of the month? In Fort McMurray? Yea... At least Edmonton is really nice though.<br /> <br /> It's exactly like all the fallout characters I make with 2-3 Luck. One person I told this to asked me what Sidereal I pissed off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man, there's nothing really you can say to that. I wish you the best.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=897384#post897384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I definitely appreciate everybody's advice to &quot;just have six Solars.&quot; I agree with all statements about the lack of mechanical overlap. Honest and for-truly. My main wish, however, is to avoid thematic overlap and to maintain a trend in my campaign wherein there's only ever one of everything.<br /> <br /> Great advice, really! And I'm open to it if there's no other choice. But it's not ideal for narrative reasons.<br /> <br /> As options go, how well do folks think a Dragon King Ochilike could hold his own with the Solar Exalted at say 150 XP? What if I started him as an Ancient?<br /> <br /> And I really do like the idea of a playable God hanging out with a circle of Solars. Are there any good conversions for Godly charms and an XP table for Gods compatible with 3E that anyone knows of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? There has -never- been inter-splat balance, in exalted, and any attempt to do so, is going to be largely a matter of ST fiat. We might be seeing the closest to 'balanced' when other 3E splats come out, but there is a very clear difference in tier. The best balance you'll get, in my (admittedly limited to three games) experience, is to cheat like hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:31:59-07:00","id":897470,"title":"","content":"Tangentially, how viable is it to play QC characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:13:53-07:00","id":897514,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'd call it very viable at all. Like even if you combine all the DB options, or Lunar options, you're still basically two or three narrow archetypes and primarily fixated on combat capability. If you're okay with that maybe, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:19:35-07:00","id":897518,"title":"","content":"What about as a deity, like a god, or an elemental? The upside would be that you can maybe come up with new powers that relate to your domain or nature on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:43:30-07:00","id":897531,"title":"","content":"QC are only made for one purpose just to make the ST job easier...its not meant to be used for player characters at all. But well, do whatever you want at your table, i guess.<br /> <br /> Gods in general are probably the worst kind of beings to have as players, Gods are literally just people working in offices and getting paid a salary by Yu Shan, and some of them have become unemployed. Gods are mostly being dick in creation, because they suddenly lose their jobs or their boss, dies for whatever reason (Shadowlands, an angry exalt? whatever you can think of ...) when a subordinate god doesn't have a boss...he ends up doing whatever, because the system was never made with the idea that the gods wouldn't have a job in the first place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:58:33-07:00","id":897804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=897518#post897518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about as a deity, like a god, or an elemental? The upside would be that you can maybe come up with new powers that relate to your domain or nature on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Free-form anything is pretty hard in Exalted. The entire system is built on discrete units of power that are built to interact with each other. Workings and Artifact creation are somewhat free-form, but they are also deliberately segregated from the normal system, and are subservient to it(Workings make things that work within the normal system, for example).<br /> <br /> In my experience, flexibility equals power in RPGs. That's why Mages tend to be scary in oWoD mixed games, even though they are arguably the &quot;weakest&quot; of the supernaturals.<br /> <br /> I think any attempt to tack on a free-form power system to Exalted is doomed to failure. At best, it works, and screws up game balance. At worst, it's lackluster and boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:17:25-07:00","id":897943,"title":"","content":"On a Side Note.. I've just Received the Book (Had the PDF for about 5 days.) And DAMN.... It's bigger then my HERO System books....<br /> <br /> Going to get into reading it in Earnest sometime in the next couple of days...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T00:20:32-07:00","id":898728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e#post896616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a slight boggle. I have a full Circle of Solars. I'd like to add another player, but I really dislike redundancy.<br /> <br /> Is there currently anything I can give him to play wherein he can hang with a Solar Circle and have enough stuff to buy and do to not be bored? I'll accept homebrews, whatever. Has anyone experimented with playable Gods?<br /> <br /> If there aren't, I'll ask my players if anyone of them is willing to share their Caste, but I'd like to avoid that if I can.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disclaimer: I didn't read the entire thread. Have you considered an Abyssal or Green Sun Prince? Their charms are based on attribute + ability like Solars (at least for now). Change the aesthetics of the Charms to match their appropriate Exalt type. It'd allow for some different backgrounds or character types at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T01:55:02-07:00","id":898761,"title":"","content":"I'm playing an abyssal in a 3rd edition game atm- the classic 2nd edition solar mirror abyssal is fairly easy to insert into the system since most of their charms are mirrors of solar ones and thus thematically appropriate charms can easily be recreated with some aesthetic and effect-related tweaks to the charms in the sourcebook (with some bans in place- my dm understandably does not allow me to pursue charm trees that focus on shielding or healing others).<br /> <br /> We're probably not the best example of homebrewing out there as we really didn't go to a lot of effort besides &quot;solar, but voidy&quot; and a lot of the stuff that is making my character stand out as an abyssal is due to roleplay (and resonance). But it's worked quiet well narratively so far, and when it comes to abyssals i play for the narrative more than anything else!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T06:56:23-07:00","id":898881,"title":"","content":"Trying to use Solar mirror effects to model Green Sun Princes would work about as well as using it to model Sidereals, which is to say the result won't resemble the 2E splat at all. But do whatever floats your boat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:29:32-07:00","id":899185,"title":"","content":"In a little aside, though certainly related, a player who's up to trying something a little weird and different could play a Twilight's demonic/elemental familiar, much like i ended up doing in a game i participate due to not only being &quot;the 6th PC&quot; but having a more irregular schedule than the rest of group, making a &quot;more NPCish&quot; concept desirable.<br /> <br /> Started as a run-of-the-mill Blood Ape, got killed along the way, &quot;ressurected&quot; in a frankensteinian way as a demon-elemental-fae-ghost thing through Ephemeral Induction Technique and probably making the jump to fully independent ally of the group through a combination of his servitude period not getting renewed and i getting more time to play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:35:53-07:00","id":899196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=896645#post896645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Alternately you could use wasteven's <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?780702-Exalted-3-Tinkering-with-a-fan-supplements-Sidereals-Where-Fate-Has-Led\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereals: Where Fate Has Lead homebrew</a>.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://41.media.tumblr.com/41233db9df480d3516429fd476f22676/tumblr_inline_o5qms9lcXB1tf7up7_540.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:06:54-07:00","id":899233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=897384#post897384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I definitely appreciate everybody's advice to &quot;just have six Solars.&quot; I agree with all statements about the lack of mechanical overlap. Honest and for-truly. My main wish, however, is to avoid thematic overlap and to maintain a trend in my campaign wherein there's only ever one of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this sixth player new to the game or edition? Because you can have him play as a mortal to ease him into the game.<br /> <br /> Though, frankly I'd call that a stopgap maneuver. If I join a game of Exalted, I'm gonna wanna play as an Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:47:01-07:00","id":899279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/896616-besides-a-solar-what-can-you-currently-play-in-3e?p=898881#post898881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to use Solar mirror effects to model Green Sun Princes would work about as well as using it to model Sidereals, which is to say the result won't resemble the 2E splat at all. But do whatever floats your boat!</div> </div> </div> </div>i wasn't suggesting modeling the Charm design of 2E GSPs but rather everything else. The devs said the GSP Charm design would be attribute + ability like Solars and Abyssals unless they've changed course on that plan. Which they could have!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:02:52-07:00","id":899302,"title":"","content":"As far as I know their plans didn't change with infernals being attribute+ability based, their special feature this time is mostly every charms that they get, they get more &quot;shintai&quot; customization options, so every infernal can customize their shintai form and abilities to their wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}